WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.304
-We now have the audio
of a damning phone call

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.606
in which Donald Trump's
former lawyer, Rudy Giuliani,

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.041
explicitly dangled
a quid pro quo

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:10.342
to pressure Ukrainian officials

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:11.777
to interfere in
the 2020 election

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:13.579
to help Trump
and hurt Joe Biden.

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:16.749
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:20.252 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:22.422
As we all know,
Rudy is currently under

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.723
what we can only assume

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.959
is a very serious
criminal investigation,

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.361
given that they raided
his home and office

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:30.196
and seized his
electronic devices.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:33.333
This investigation could
very well land Rudy in jail.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.933
According to another
former Trump associate

00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:36.235
who's already been there.

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.237 line:0%
-Investigating Donald Trump,
as prosecutors ramp up

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:40.406 line:0%
their investigation
into the former president.

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:43.109
Another name always comes up,
doesn't it?

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.210
Rudy Giuliani.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.312
Could the former mayor
end up in prison?

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:50.416
-The FBI is not raiding his home

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:54.687
without having extremely
significant documentation,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.457
information within which
to pursue this.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.724
There's no way in the world

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:00.193
that they're going to
let him off the hook.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.461
What Rudy needs to do
is like what I did --

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:05.998
you need to take responsibility
for what you did wrong.

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:07.433
What Rudy needs to do --

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:11.904
and this is my speech to Rudy
and to anybody else --

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:13.139
they have him,

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:16.275
and so if he's looking
to protect himself

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:17.644
so that he doesn't end up

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:20.580
spending the rest
of his life in prison,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.149
he may want to actually
start to cooperate.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.784
-Somehow,
Michael Cohen has become

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:27.620
the wise, elder statesman
of former Trump goons.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.156
He used to be the intimidating
Mafia-style bag man,

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.158
and now he's like
a guidance counselor

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.794
sitting backwards on a chair
to give Rudy a pep talk.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.029
"You've got to straighten
out your life, man.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:38.331
You could be somebody,

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.200
but if you keep hanging out
with the wrong crowd,

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.770
you're going to find yourself
working down at the gas station

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.171
for the rest of your life."

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.274
"But I love the gas station.
That's where I get my hair dye."

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.042
It's fitting that Cohen
looks like

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:52.578
a bargain bin Ray Romano now,
because he sounds like

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.413
he's giving brotherly advice
to Robert.

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:55.615
[ As Ray Romano ] "Oh, Robert,

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:58.050
you got to take responsibility
for what you do.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.586
You got to tell Ma
you broke her vase."

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.922
"Raymond, don't tell mom
about the vase, Raymond."

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.091 line:0%
And we have heard the feedback

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.226 line:0%
and understand those impressions
are polarizing,

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:10.629 line:0%
so do please go to
@seacaptainpolls on Twitter,

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:13.532 line:0%
where you can either vote
"Everybody loves Seth's Raymond"

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:15.701 line:0%
or "Everybody hates fun."

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:16.836
So if you take Cohen's
word for it,

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.805
Rudy could very well
end up in jail.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:22.374
And I know we've been saying
some version of that sentence

00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:25.244
about a bunch of different Trump
cronies for over four years,

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:28.381
and yet somehow it feels like
they all evade accountability.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:31.483 line:0%
I mean, Steve Bannon's out there
just doing a podcast

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:33.919 line:0%
like a 22-year-old stand-up,
and looking like

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:36.222 line:0%
he's about to film a scene
in the new "Aquaman"

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:39.826 line:0%
where he plays, I don't know,
a guy who guards the sea cave,

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.660 line:0%
despite the fact
that he got arrested

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.596 line:0%
by the Postal Service
police force

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.698 line:0%
on a Chinese
billionaire's yacht,

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.966 line:0%
an insane thing
that actually happened,

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.401 line:0%
and not, as I first thought,

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.370 line:0%
a lyric from the Don Henley
song "Boys of Summer."

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.839 line:0%
I mean, he got arrested
by postal cops

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.940 line:0%
at a Chinese
billionaire's yacht.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.643 line:0%
♪ Don't look back,
you can never look back ♪

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.478 line:0%
That probably won't even make it
into the history books

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:01.480 line:0%
about the Trump era, because
there's just too much to cover.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:02.582 line:0%
And it's such a bummer,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:05.084 line:0%
because there should be
an entire chapter

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.385 line:0%
devoted to the fact

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:09.121 line:0%
that the Postal Service
has a police force.

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:11.357 line:0%
Personally, if I were
in high school,

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.226 line:0%
I'd be psyched to learn there
are Postal Service cops.

00:03:14.226 --> 00:03:15.995 line:0%
If I found out about that
in 10th grade history class.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.930 line:0%
there's a good chance
I'd be out there right now,

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.631 line:0%
walking the beat
in those short shorts

00:03:19.631 --> 00:03:21.701 line:0%
with my bucket hat
and a badge,

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.971 line:0%
solving mail crimes with
my unorthodox method,

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.073 line:0%
and Chief would always
be trying to muzzle me, saying,

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.941 line:0%
"Meyers, I got the mayor
breathing down my neck

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:30.042 line:0%
thanks to your stunt."

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:31.510
And I'd say,
"What am I supposed to do,

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.080
just cram the whole Pottery Barn
catalog through that tiny slot?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.181
I had to break those windows."

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.882
And he'd say,
"You're gonna fly right,

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:37.983
or I'll have your badge."

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:39.451
And I'd say to him,
"Sorry, Chief,

00:03:39.451 --> 00:03:41.186
but I'm like an envelope
with photos inside.

00:03:41.186 --> 00:03:43.723
I do not bend."

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.823
You know, I should probably stop

00:03:44.823 --> 00:03:46.659
before I give away
the entire plot

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.894
for my new collaboration
with Dick Wolf,

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:51.197
"Chicago Postal Service
Police Force."

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.665
[ One chord of "Law &amp; Order"
theme plays ]

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:56.035
The cheapskates at NBC would
only pay for one of the "dun"s.

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:00.272
"Chicago Postal Service
Police Force"

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:01.674
is just one of the many ways,

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.676
along with my new company,
MyZipper,

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.144
and my Broadway musicals,
"Cicada, Cicada,"

00:04:06.144 --> 00:04:09.715
that I'm soon going to be the
richest man in the world.

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:11.417
Anyway,
what was I talking about?

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.653
Oh, right. Rudy Giuliani.
[ Chuckling ]

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:15.688
So, who knows?

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:16.722
Maybe Cohen's wrong,

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:18.490
and Rudy will end up fine
like the others,

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.059
but I just can't imagine
the feds

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.328
raiding Rudy Giuliani's
home and office

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.662
and finding nothing
incriminating.

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:25.965
I mean, forget Ukraine
and quid pro quos.

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.366
He's probably got
a fridge full of

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:29.135
whitefish he stole from Zabar's

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:31.504
or a sink full of
unpaid parking tickets

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.940
he tried to stuff into
the garbage disposal,

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.308
only to remember
he doesn't have one.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:38.077
He's probably breaking all kinds
of co-op board rules, too,

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:40.446
especially with that
welcome mat.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:41.613
And you know
he probably has neighbors

00:04:41.613 --> 00:04:43.116
that are happy to rat on him --

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.617
maybe a guy who,
and I'm just spitballing here,

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:47.153
is in a bathrobe and a Yankees
head who's eating a bagel.

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:50.022
"Hey, you guys looking
in Rudy's apartment?

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:53.493
Yeah, okay, because last week
he woke me up at 3:00 a.m.

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:57.063
He asked me to hold this Bitcoin
for him in case the cops came.

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.765
It was just a duffel bag
of old subway tokens.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:04.237
Also, do you know
he married his cousin?"

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.638
One sign that
the investigation is serious

00:05:06.638 --> 00:05:09.175
is that federal agents
seized his electronic devices,

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.843
and apparently he had
a lot of them.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.845
According to a court
filing last month,

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.480
prosecutors seized
18 electronic devices,

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.684
including phones and computers
belonging to Giuliani,

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:21.220
as well as certain
employees of his firm.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.589
Alright, first of all,
what 77-year-old man

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.425
has that many
electronic devices?

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.992
"Yeah, Chief,
we found three phones,

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:30.329
two iPads,
a Palm Pilot, an Atari 2600,

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:31.764
three blood pressure cuffs --"

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:34.000
"Meyers, I thought I told you
you were off this case."

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.369
"The Postal Service Police Force
are never off the case!"

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:38.237
[ One chord of "Law &amp; Order"
theme plays ]

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:41.807
Was that the same "dun,"
or the back "dun?"

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:45.611
So I can only get
each one one time?

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:48.814
Also, I'm sorry,
Rudy Giuliani has employees?

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:50.516
Can you imagine working
for this guy?

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.184
"Hey, honey, I'm going
to be home late tonight.

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:54.420
Yeah, the boss thought
he had reservations at Morton's,

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:58.223
but it just turns out
he bought some salt.

00:05:58.223 --> 00:06:01.260
I'm laughing, too."

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.329
I can't picture Rudy actually
being in charge of people.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:04.697
When I imagine him
employing someone,

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:07.299
I just assume he pulls aside
a kid on the street

00:06:07.299 --> 00:06:09.335
and flips them a nickel
to run an errand for him

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.637
like he's Chazz Palminteri
in "A Bronx Tale."

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.406
"Hey, kid, take this briefcase
full of cash down to the docks.

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:17.510
You come back alive, I might
have something bigger for you."

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.846
And now we may be getting
a better idea

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:21.913
of what exactly federal agents
might have found

00:06:21.913 --> 00:06:23.282
on all those devices.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.984
Let's first take a trip
down memory lane,

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:26.552
back to the first impeachment
of Donald Trump.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.954
You might remember
the central allegation

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:31.023
that during
an official phone call

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.357
with the president of Ukraine,

00:06:32.357 --> 00:06:34.760
Trump had tried
to extort Ukraine

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.729
and get them to interfere
in the 2020 election

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.096
by digging up dirt on Biden.

00:06:38.096 --> 00:06:40.766
We all read the transcript,
where it was very clear

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:43.268
that what Trump was doing
was dangling a quid pro quo.

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:45.004
And yet Trump denied it,

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:47.506
uttering the same refrain
so many times,

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:49.675
it almost started to sound like
a religious mantra

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:52.377
you would hear on the street
from some weird cult member

00:06:52.377 --> 00:06:53.612
trying to convert you.

00:06:53.612 --> 00:06:57.350
-There was no quid pro quo.
There was nothing.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:00.753
There was no
quid pro quo at all.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:04.957
If you remember at the
beginning, it was quid pro quo.

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:09.595
But listen to this --
there is no pro quo.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:10.762
-That sounds like
something you'd say

00:07:10.762 --> 00:07:12.298
when you get stopped
on your way to work

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:14.200
by some German tourists
in Times Square.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.202
"Excuse me, can you tell us
where to find the M&amp;M store?"

00:07:17.202 --> 00:07:18.971
"Uh, scusi. No pro quo."

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:21.007
Ah, the good old days, huh?

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:23.709
So quaint, back when the biggest
scandal in politics

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:25.744
was the president trying
to extort a foreign country,

00:07:25.744 --> 00:07:28.313
before we were all trapped
in our homes for a year

00:07:28.313 --> 00:07:29.548
to avoid a deadly plague

00:07:29.548 --> 00:07:31.783
and a violent mob
tried to overthrow democracy.

00:07:31.783 --> 00:07:34.553
♪ Don't look back,
you can never look back ♪

00:07:34.553 --> 00:07:35.687
Look, I'm sorry

00:07:35.687 --> 00:07:37.856
all my references lately
are for 50-year-old men,

00:07:37.856 --> 00:07:40.692
but look at my audience
right now.

00:07:40.692 --> 00:07:42.027
I mean, I bring
in younger people,

00:07:42.027 --> 00:07:43.862
but their little hands
can't hold all the cue cards.

00:07:43.862 --> 00:07:46.365
Now obviously, you don't
have to be a lawyer

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:48.734
to guess that a quid pro quo
sounds super illegal,

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:51.437
so that was their line --
there was no quid pro quo.

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:54.606
But now we have damning
new audiotapes of a phone call

00:07:54.606 --> 00:07:57.776
Rudy Giuliani had with
a Ukrainian official in 2019

00:07:57.776 --> 00:08:00.713
in which it definitely sounds
like there was a quid pro quo.

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:05.217
-CNN today obtained audio of
a 2019 phone conversation

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:08.020
between Rudy Giuliani

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:11.290
and an adviser
to the president of Ukraine.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.825
In that conversation,
which again, took place in 2019,

00:08:13.825 --> 00:08:15.560
Mr. Giuliani can be heard

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.830
pressuring
the Ukrainian government

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.266
that their president
must publicly announce

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:25.938
a sham investigation into some
alleged wrongdoing by Joe Biden.

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:28.574
-The audio obtained
exclusively by CNN

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:30.976
is from a roughly 40-minute call

00:08:30.976 --> 00:08:35.014
between Giuliani, a US diplomat,
and a Ukrainian official.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:36.849
-Alright, first of all,
how is it that

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:39.184
every time these guys do
something shady or illegal,

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:40.386
they get caught on tape?

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:42.421
At this point,
they're less like politicians

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:43.756
and more like Twitch streamers.

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:46.091
"Hey, guys, Brad here,
about to bribe a foreign country

00:08:46.091 --> 00:08:47.292
to interfere in our elections.

00:08:47.292 --> 00:08:48.894
Figured I'd go live.

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:50.529
Also I'm gonna try
another speedrun

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:51.964
on 'Super Mario Brothers.'

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:53.632
I keep getting eaten
by the chain chomp,

00:08:53.632 --> 00:08:57.269
which totally blows."

00:08:57.269 --> 00:08:59.304
We on purpose didn't
give Wally lines today,

00:08:59.304 --> 00:09:01.573
because when we do,
we have to pay him extra money,

00:09:01.573 --> 00:09:04.376
and I'm trying to save
as much money as possible

00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:08.013
so that NBC will let me
buy an M.C. Hammer sample,

00:09:08.013 --> 00:09:10.682
and I'm getting
as creative as I can.

00:09:10.682 --> 00:09:12.585
Like the other day,
I brought our budget

00:09:12.585 --> 00:09:14.353
to our line producer, Jen,
and I said,

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:16.421
"Hey, right here there's
all this money for suits,

00:09:16.421 --> 00:09:17.890
and I'm not wearing
suits anymore.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.759
So couldn't we use that money
to pay for M.C. Hammer?"

00:09:20.759 --> 00:09:21.994
And she just looked at it,

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:23.495
and you know
what she said to me?

00:09:23.495 --> 00:09:25.063
"You can't touch this."

00:09:25.063 --> 00:09:27.099
[ No music playing ]

00:09:31.236 --> 00:09:33.305
Also, my sympathies
to the Ukrainian official.

00:09:33.305 --> 00:09:36.809
This call was 40 minutes long.
40 minutes.

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:38.944
If I'm on the phone
for more than three minutes,

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:40.278
it ruins my entire day.

00:09:40.278 --> 00:09:41.880
The only time I've ever
on the phone that long

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:43.082
is if I'm fighting with

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:45.718
the automated customer service
agent at Verizon.

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:47.286
I just want to
cancel my service!

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:49.655
-I heard you want to
upgrade your service.

00:09:49.655 --> 00:09:50.656
Is that right?

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:52.758
-No, I said cancel my service.

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:55.828
-I heard you want to add stars
for $15 a month.

00:09:55.828 --> 00:09:56.861
Is that right?

00:09:56.861 --> 00:09:58.697
-No, I want to cancel.

00:09:58.697 --> 00:10:02.167
-I heard you want to purchase
"Wedding Crashers 2" on demand.

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:03.302
Is that right?

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:05.838
-Yes, I do.

00:10:05.838 --> 00:10:08.173
Can we just take
a moment to acknowledge

00:10:08.173 --> 00:10:10.609
that the rumors
of a "Wedding Crashers" sequel

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:13.212
are finally gaining steam,
mere months after

00:10:13.212 --> 00:10:15.414
we started referencing
the original on this show

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:16.548
for literally no reason?

00:10:16.548 --> 00:10:18.150
Well, not no reason.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.818
The reason is there's
no audience here

00:10:19.818 --> 00:10:21.086
to say, "Jesus enough."

00:10:21.086 --> 00:10:23.955
Still, you're welcome.

00:10:23.955 --> 00:10:26.458
I don't know much about
how the sequel got started,

00:10:26.458 --> 00:10:28.494
but I bet the conversation was
a little something like this --

00:10:28.494 --> 00:10:29.962
[ As Vince Vaughn ]
"Buddy, buddy, buddy.

00:10:29.962 --> 00:10:32.131
We got to shoot this sequel.
People have waited long enough.

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:33.732
They want to know
if we're still crashing."

00:10:33.732 --> 00:10:34.734
[ As Owen Wilson ]
"I'm not sure, man.

00:10:34.734 --> 00:10:35.968
I feel like we'd be messing

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:37.569
with the integrity
of the original."

00:10:37.569 --> 00:10:39.305
Anyway, where was I?

00:10:39.305 --> 00:10:43.408
Oh, right. Rudy.

00:10:43.408 --> 00:10:45.577
The fact that the phone call
is 40 minutes long

00:10:45.577 --> 00:10:48.280
means there's lots of
damning stuff in there.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:50.816
For example,
Rudy had this insane theory

00:10:50.816 --> 00:10:52.517
that it was actually Ukraine

00:10:52.517 --> 00:10:55.454
that interfered in
the 2016 election to hurt Trump,

00:10:55.454 --> 00:10:56.856
and he wanted
Ukrainian officials

00:10:56.856 --> 00:10:58.524
to investigate that theory.

00:10:58.524 --> 00:11:01.594
-Way back in last November,

00:11:01.594 --> 00:11:06.399
I got information from
a reliable investigator,

00:11:06.399 --> 00:11:09.568
international investigator,

00:11:09.568 --> 00:11:14.006
that there was a certain amount
of activity in Ukraine

00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:17.176
during the 2016 election

00:11:17.176 --> 00:11:23.782
that was, that involved
Ukrainian officials

00:11:23.782 --> 00:11:25.417
and Ukrainian --

00:11:25.417 --> 00:11:31.323
mostly officials
being asked by our embassy

00:11:31.323 --> 00:11:34.526
possibly by other
American officials.

00:11:34.526 --> 00:11:40.766
Basically, I mean, the statement
was to produce dirt

00:11:40.766 --> 00:11:45.604
on then-candidate Trump
and Paul Manafort.

00:11:45.604 --> 00:11:46.839
-I have a feeling I know who

00:11:46.839 --> 00:11:49.107
this international
investigator was.

00:11:49.107 --> 00:11:50.575
[ As Mike Lindell ]
"That -- that would be me.

00:11:50.575 --> 00:11:51.977
I'm the one who told Rudy

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:54.713
Ukraine interfered
in the election to hurt Trump.

00:11:54.713 --> 00:11:58.217
I heard it from Sidney Powell
and Hugo Chavez

00:11:58.217 --> 00:12:01.754
in a secret meeting that was
recorded by Italian satellites.

00:12:01.754 --> 00:12:05.724
But also, you got to remember,
I'm real tired all the time

00:12:05.724 --> 00:12:09.127
because my pillow sucks.
plus I sleep in the woods,

00:12:09.127 --> 00:12:14.467
and I got really nervous
because of all the bears."

00:12:14.467 --> 00:12:18.404
So that's -- let's see, that's
Lindell, Vaughn, Wilson, Romano.

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:20.539
Did the Smithsonian
ask for anything else,

00:12:20.539 --> 00:12:22.475
or can we just send this over?

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.679
I'd sell an NFT
of this "Closer Look,"

00:12:27.679 --> 00:12:30.349
but I already got
too much money.

00:12:32.751 --> 00:12:34.286
But then Rudy got down
to business

00:12:34.286 --> 00:12:37.056
and made it clear
that what he and Trump wanted

00:12:37.056 --> 00:12:39.424
was for Ukraine's president
to make a public statement

00:12:39.424 --> 00:12:43.462
declaring that they were opening
an investigation into Joe Biden.

00:12:43.462 --> 00:12:45.731
-What we need, all we need
from the president is

00:12:45.731 --> 00:12:49.567
to say, "I'm gonna put an
honest prosecutor in charge.

00:12:49.567 --> 00:12:54.073
He's going to investigate
and dig up the evidence

00:12:54.073 --> 00:12:58.377
that presently exists,
and is there any other evidence

00:12:58.377 --> 00:13:02.414
about involvement
of the 2016 election."

00:13:02.414 --> 00:13:06.518
And then the Biden thing
has to be run out.

00:13:06.518 --> 00:13:08.086
I don't know
if it's true or not.

00:13:08.086 --> 00:13:09.187
-No, you don't.

00:13:09.187 --> 00:13:10.688
These guys can't even
bring themselves

00:13:10.688 --> 00:13:11.723
to believe their own B.S.

00:13:11.723 --> 00:13:12.992
This is how they always do it.

00:13:12.992 --> 00:13:15.661
They float insane theories
and then cover themselves

00:13:15.661 --> 00:13:17.195
by saying they're
just asking questions,

00:13:17.195 --> 00:13:19.765
like they're gossipy
high school sophomores.

00:13:19.765 --> 00:13:21.233
"You need to break up
with Todd ASAP,

00:13:21.233 --> 00:13:23.301
because I heard he went to
Jenny's lake house last weekend

00:13:23.301 --> 00:13:24.837
and told Brad
that Karen told Michael,

00:13:24.837 --> 00:13:26.805
who told Emma's teammate's
cousin's brother's mom

00:13:26.805 --> 00:13:27.840
that she has a crush on him.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.041
I don't know if it's true."

00:13:29.041 --> 00:13:31.210
And it was clear
what they were doing was shady

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:33.212
and that they knew
it was shady,

00:13:33.212 --> 00:13:36.448
because they all talk in
that vague, Mafia-esque tone

00:13:36.448 --> 00:13:38.651
where they never actually
demand something explicitly,

00:13:38.651 --> 00:13:40.051
but they make it very clear

00:13:40.051 --> 00:13:42.387
that what they're asking for
is a quid pro quo.

00:13:42.387 --> 00:13:46.058
-If he could make some
statement at the right time

00:13:46.058 --> 00:13:51.163
that he supports a fair,
honest law enforcement system

00:13:51.163 --> 00:13:55.301
and that these investigations
go wherever they have to go,

00:13:55.301 --> 00:13:57.702
it's gonna be
run by honest people,

00:13:57.702 --> 00:13:59.805
that would probably
clear the air really well.

00:13:59.805 --> 00:14:04.276
And I think it would
make it possible for me to come,

00:14:04.276 --> 00:14:07.879
and make it possible, I think,
for me to talk to the President

00:14:07.879 --> 00:14:11.216
and see what I can do about
making sure

00:14:11.216 --> 00:14:14.219
that whatever misunderstandings
are put aside.

00:14:14.219 --> 00:14:19.358
And maybe even, I kind of think
that this could be a good thing

00:14:19.358 --> 00:14:22.961
for having
a much better relationship,

00:14:22.961 --> 00:14:24.830
where we really
understand each other.

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:28.800
If he could say
something like that on his own,

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:33.972
in conversation,
it would go a long way

00:14:33.972 --> 00:14:38.243
with the President
to solve the problems.

00:14:38.243 --> 00:14:40.245
-"It would go a long way
to solve the problems."

00:14:40.245 --> 00:14:42.081
Rudy sounds like he should
be wearing a track suit

00:14:42.081 --> 00:14:43.715
and running his fingertip
along the bar

00:14:43.715 --> 00:14:45.050
at a New Jersey restaurant
saying,

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:47.185
"This is a nice place --
nice and flammable,

00:14:47.185 --> 00:14:48.654
if you know what I mean."

00:14:48.654 --> 00:14:51.589
Also, I love that Rudy's reward
for their cooperation

00:14:51.589 --> 00:14:53.625
was saying that he
would personally

00:14:53.625 --> 00:14:54.960
visit them in Ukraine.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:57.663
I'm sure they were psyched
about the idea of Rudy

00:14:57.663 --> 00:14:59.965
showing up at their door,
asking to sleep on their futon,

00:14:59.965 --> 00:15:01.400
and then spending three days

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.135
talking about cigars
and the Yankees

00:15:03.135 --> 00:15:05.637
and asking them where to find
the best salami in Kiev.

00:15:05.637 --> 00:15:07.039
"I'm jonesing for some Genoa.

00:15:07.039 --> 00:15:09.107
Mind if I put my cigar
out on your rug?"

00:15:09.107 --> 00:15:10.809
This whole thing is
yet another reminder

00:15:10.809 --> 00:15:13.478
of the central thrust of
Republican politics right now --

00:15:13.478 --> 00:15:15.114
cheating in elections to win.

00:15:15.114 --> 00:15:17.516
They made it clear they'll do it
any way they can,

00:15:17.516 --> 00:15:19.718
whether it's using
the levers of the state

00:15:19.718 --> 00:15:22.521
to pressure government officials
to overturn elections,

00:15:22.521 --> 00:15:25.657
passing voter suppression laws,
or extorting foreign countries.

00:15:25.657 --> 00:15:27.526
They didn't stop
after the Ukraine scandal,

00:15:27.526 --> 00:15:28.694
and they're not stopping now.

00:15:28.694 --> 00:15:30.996
It turns out the biggest
criminals are the ones

00:15:30.996 --> 00:15:32.664
in the so-called party
of law and order.

00:15:32.664 --> 00:15:34.333
[ Two chords of "Law &amp; Order"
theme plays ]

00:15:34.333 --> 00:15:35.333
Oh, the gave them both.

00:15:35.333 --> 00:15:36.902
This has been "A Closer Look."

